  "id": "COMPOUND:192 - DISEASE:1932",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link between succinylcholine and Macrostomia, mediated through the coiled-coil domain containing 33 (CCD33) protein. Succinylcholine, a neuromuscular blocker, is shown to affect CCD33, which in turn is implicated in multiple conditions, including Hypophosphatemic rickets, Melanoma-Pancreatic cancer syndrome, and Glaucoma 1, open angle, O. These conditions are all associated with CCD33 dysfunction, and the shared pathway to Macrostomia indicates a possible role for CCD33 in the development or maintenance of this condition. The evidence suggests that succinylcholine may modulate CCD33 activity, potentially influencing the pathophysiology of Macrostomia. The integration of multiple paths highlights a consistent mechanism involving CCD33, though the exact nature of the interaction between succinylcholine and CCD33 remains to be fully elucidated. The observed association is supported by a recurring pathway involving CCD33 and Macrostomia, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the therapeutic relevance.",
